Subject: [Krypton] Complete the direct Chrome Web Store download protocol

Krypton downloads from the store directly rather than Helium's proxy. Keep
Helium's fixed platform query and disabled usage pings, but send the actual
browser version: without prodversion the store returns HTTP 204 instead of
a CRX, which surfaces as "Download interrupted". Restore the canonical
store update URL so download trust checks and gallery/update classification
recognize the direct endpoint. Do not broaden off-store installation rules.

--- a/components/update_client/update_query_params.cc
+++ b/components/update_client/update_query_params.cc
@@ -87,7 +87,9 @@
 // static
 std::string UpdateQueryParams::Get(ProdId prod) {
   if (prod == CRX_DUMMY) {
-    return "os=win&arch=x64&prod=chromecrx&acceptformat=crx3,puff";
+    return absl::StrFormat(
+        "os=win&arch=x64&prod=chromecrx&prodversion=%s&acceptformat=crx3,puff",
+        GetProdVersion());
   }
 
   return absl::StrFormat("os=%s&arch=%s&prod=%s%s&acceptformat=crx3,puff", kOs,
